# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Lure forces every eligible creature to block Tangle Asp, whose delayed triggers destroy those blockers at end of combat.
# Forcing: Two opposing ground creatures are both eligible, and a -1/-1 counter makes the Asp assign no combat damage.
# AI behavior: After Lure resolves, both blockers must be assigned to the sole attacker.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = Both blockers and Tangle Asp leave the battlefield, with the blockers destroyed only by delayed triggers.
#   LOSE = A blocker remains because forced blocking or the delayed destruction failed.
#   TIMEOUT = Block declaration, damage assignment, or end-of-combat triggers fail to converge.
# Card roles:
#   Lure — forces every eligible opposing creature to block the enchanted attacker.
#   Tangle Asp — zero-power attacker and source of one delayed destruction trigger per blocker.
#   Grizzly Bears — first eligible blocker.
#   Centaur Courser — second eligible blocker and proof that the restriction applies to all candidates.
# Protocol path: Aura cast and targeting, attachment, attacker declaration, forced blocker legality, combat damage, delayed trigger lifecycle, and zone transfers.

